## Model card

- **Name:** Gemini 2.5 Pro
- **Short description:** Google’s Gemini 2.5 Pro is a deprecated earlier-generation thinking model for complex reasoning, coding, STEM, and long-context analysis, now being superseded/routed toward newer Gemini models.
- **Provider / access:** Google AI Studio / Gemini API and Vertex AI surfaces (per Google AI developer docs). Local metadata lists `opencode/gemini-2.5-pro` and `noFreeId`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Google AI developer docs list latest update June 2025 and knowledge cutoff January 2025.
- **IDs:** `gemini-2.5-pro`.
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 input tokens; 65,536 output tokens (Google AI developer docs). Local metadata states 1,048,576 (1M); 64K out.
- **Modalities:** Audio, images, video, text, and PDF input; text output (Google AI developer docs).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** Developer docs reference pricing page; local metadata lists $1.25/$10.00 per 1M (<=200K prompts) and $2.50/$15.00 (>200K). Specific current pricing details not fully extracted from reviewed docs in this pass.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary Google/DeepMind model; architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

